---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import fontAwesomeLicense from '../../../LICENSES/LicenseRef-FontAwesome-Free.txt?raw';
import octiconsLicense from '../../../LICENSES/LicenseRef-Octicons-MIT.txt?raw';
import logos from '../assets/logos/catalog.json';
---
<Base title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Read-only package monitoring for <a href="https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/openRuyi">openRuyi</a>, a rolling Linux distribution for RISC-V.</p>

    <h2>Reading conventions</h2>
    <dl class="api-list">
      <dt>Version</dt>
      <dd>RPM-expanded SPEC version → tracked upstream target. Comparison excludes Epoch and Release. Untracked means no upstream version rule.</dd>
      <dt>Builds</dt>
      <dd>Results belong to individual OBS targets. Success does not confirm delivery of the current source. A different last-successful version remains visible.</dd>
      <dt>Labels and checks</dt>
      <dd>CheckFailed means collection failed, not the build. Package details show evidence and failed checks.</dd>
      <dt>Time and scope</dt>
      <dd>Collection and build timestamps differ. Failed checks can retain older observations. Advisory matches do not account for local patches.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <dl class="api-list">
      <dt>Source and builds</dt>
      <dd><a href="https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/openRuyi/tree/main/SPECS">openRuyi SPEC files</a> provide package metadata; <a href="https://build.openruyi.cn/">BuildService</a> provides target states and build history.</dd>
      <dt>Versions</dt>
      <dd><a href="https://nvchecker.readthedocs.io/">nvchecker</a> queries configured upstream releases, registries and repositories. Rules select identities and release lines.</dd>
      <dt>Dependencies, licenses and withdrawn releases</dt>
      <dd>Upstream registries and release metadata, including PyPI, crates.io, Go module services and MetaCPAN. Coverage depends on the source and package identity.</dd>
      <dt>Security</dt>
      <dd><a href="https://osv.dev/">OSV</a>, <a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/">NVD</a> provide advisory matches; <a href="https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog">CISA KEV</a> and <a href="https://www.first.org/epss/">FIRST EPSS</a> add exploitation signals.</dd>
      <dt>Lifecycle and activity</dt>
      <dd><a href="https://endoflife.date/">endoflife.date</a> provides lifecycle dates. GitHub provides issues, pull requests and changed paths used for package associations.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p><a href="/api/v2/status">Collection status</a>: coverage and errors. <a href="/api">API</a>: observations and queries.</p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p><a href="/LICENSE.txt">MulanPSL-2.0 license</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/openRuyi-logo">openRuyi logo</a> © 2026 ISCAS and openRuyi Project Contributors. Used unchanged under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</p>
    <p>Activity icons: <a href="https://github.com/primer/octicons">GitHub Primer Octicons</a>, used unchanged under the <a href="https://github.com/primer/octicons/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a>.</p>
    <details><summary>Octicons license</summary><pre>{octiconsLicense}</pre></details>
    <p>Build icons: <a href="https://fontawesome.com/">Font Awesome Free 6.7.2</a> by Fonticons, Inc., used unchanged under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.</p>
    <details><summary>Font Awesome notices</summary><pre>{fontAwesomeLicense}</pre></details>
    <h3>Tool and ecosystem marks</h3>
    <p>Marks identify tools or language families, not endorsement. GNU identifies the Autotools family; language marks do not identify a particular build backend.</p>
    <p>Python and the Python logos are trademarks or registered trademarks of the Python Software Foundation, used under its nominative-use policy.</p>
    <p>CMake is a Kitware trademark, used only to identify the build tool; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p>
    <dl class="api-list">
      {Object.values(logos).map(logo => <><dt><a href={logo.source}>{logo.title}</a></dt><dd>{logo.credit}. <a href={logo.license_url}>{logo.license}</a>. <a href={logo.asset_source}>SVG source</a>. {logo.changes} {'trademark_url' in logo && <a href={logo.trademark_url}>Trademark policy</a>}</dd></>)}
    </dl>
  </article>
</Base>
